# Line endings for the certificate formats.
#
# `asserted.tsv`, `derivations.tsv`, `rules.tsv`, `horn.tsv` and the model and
# refutation files are tab separated with LF endings, and their parsers REFUSE a
# carriage return rather than strip one, because a CR inside a field would become
# part of an RDF term and the certificate would then be about a term nobody
# wrote. That refusal is deliberate and is what the error message says.
#
# Git's default on Windows checks text files out with CRLF, so without this the
# committed fixtures arrive carrying exactly the character the parser exists to
# reject, and the Windows CI leg fails on a file that is correct in the
# repository. Pin the working-tree ending rather than loosening the parser: the
# strictness is the feature.
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.nt  text eol=lf
*.nq  text eol=lf

# RDF serialisations, for the same reason: a stray CR changes a literal.
*.ttl text eol=lf
*.trig text eol=lf
